``nested-min-max`` no longer suggests splatting (``*``) arguments that come from
an inner ``min``/``max`` call comparing several sequences. The sequences are
compared as whole objects, so the previous suggestion changed the result, e.g.
``max([1, 2], max([3, 4], [5, 6]))`` was rewritten to the non-equivalent
``max(*[1, 2], *[3, 4], *[5, 6])``.

Refs #11590
